From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 11:49:50 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] tests: m16-check.sh, the -m16/-mregparm/.code16-.code64
 verification

tests/m16-check.sh [codegen|asm|files|regparm|link|all] compares against
GCC and GNU as on the Linux x86 boot code (needs the kernel build
directory with the gcc-built objects, KBUILD/KSRC): the -m16 and -m32
instruction streams of arch/x86/boot/*.c, the encodings of 170-odd
snippets per mode, the kernel's mixed-mode .S files section by section,
the regparm ABI at run time, and the setup.ld link with GNU ld.
